Modified on 2026-10-24 for Noki. Runtime version: 1.14.1-extended-2.7.2-nokinv-11.
Modifications: native VLESS/Hysteria2 user lifecycle and private control socket; TLS certificate reload ownership;
bounded outbound delay measurement, WireGuard key generation and private command-service state;
CPU preference expressed using existing runtime and golang.org/x/sys/cpu flags.
DNS hijack uses native user accounting and joins response callbacks before final drain.
Original license terms and copyright notices follow.

PC Windows DNS delta: scoped Dnscache WFP permits, preserved system resolver selection,
WinDivert TCP/UDP DNS interception through the existing DNSRouter, per-interface
gVisor stacks, kernel-reserved upstream source ports and independent crash cleanup.
src/pc-patches/tun_windows.go.patch replaces only tun_windows.go in the verified
github.com/sagernet/sing-tun v0.9.3 build copy; upstream file SHA-256:
998d7e712c3d830055c106397f80e797d412a13d1e7d0766b3326d47051ae010.
sing-tun source: https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-tun/tree/v0.9.3
sing-tun copyright notices and GPL-3.0-or-later license remain in the module.
The shared module cache and Android source are not modified.
No NRPT rules are published. Startup removes only legacy Noki rules, preserving
foreign policy and removing an empty GP container only after owned-rule cleanup.
The capture owner leaves TUN DNS unassigned while strict-route DNS blocking stays
active. Scoped WFP permits are installed only after capture and independent DROP
guards, and are revoked before capture shutdown.
Local file logs use two bounded 5 MiB segments and buffered writes, flush errors
immediately, and append startup failures through the same log factory.
Core UDP packet listeners preserve reserved DNS source ports. Proxy transports
retain the default-interface path; destination routing applies only to direct
outbounds using their existing DirectOutbound marker. Explicit binds stay intact.

